<h1>draw_point</h1>
<p>With this function you can draw a single pixel anywhere on the screen, using the currently set draw colour and alpha.</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code">draw_point(x, y);</p>
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th>Argument</th><th>Type</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>x</td><td><span data-keyref="Type_Real"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Real</a></span></td>
<td>The x coordinate of the point to be drawn.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>y</td><td><span data-keyref="Type_Real"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Real</a></span></td>
<td>The y coordinate of the point to be drawn.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Void">N/A</span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">draw_set_colour(c_yellow);<br/> draw_point(100,100);
</p>
<p>This will draw a yellow pixel at position (100,100).</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
